1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,961
It's never too late it's never too late to change your life it's never too late to start something new.
永远不算晚，改变生活、开始新事物都不算晚，这是她的鼓励。

2
00:00:04,961 --> 00:00:08,761
You don't need to have it all figured out in fact nobody has it all figured out.
你不必把一切都想明白；其实没有谁真的全都弄清楚了。

3
00:00:08,761 --> 00:00:12,871
Which leads me to my first point failing fast is a mindset.
这引出了她的第一点：尽早经历失败，是一种心态。

4
00:00:12,881 --> 00:00:15,640
It's a mindset that is important for so many reason.
她认为这种心态在许多方面都很重要。

5
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:22,481
You're probably thinking why would anyone want to fail it's humiliating it sucks you have to start over.
你可能会想，谁会愿意失败？很丢脸、很糟，还得重新开始。

6
00:00:22,481 --> 00:00:26,121
But I need you to understand that is a good thing.
但她希望你理解，她认为这反而是好事。

7
00:00:26,121 --> 00:00:34,151
The faster you fail because look no matter if someone seems to have life figured out they're going to fail at some point.
不管别人看起来多么掌握人生，某个时候也会遇到失败。

8
00:00:34,161 --> 00:00:40,670
We all are we're going to fail at on a small level on a big level many times throughout our lifetime here on earth.
我们都会在一生中多次失败，有小挫折，也有大挫折。

9
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:49,841
That is just inevitable I need you to understand that and the faster you can fail the faster you get to where you need to be.
她说失败不可避免，而更早经历失败，也可能更早走向你要去的地方。

10
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:56,360
Reframe your mindset on failure I know failure is scary but the more that you fail the less scarier it becomes.
重新看待失败。她知道失败令人害怕，但认为经历越多就越不害怕。

11
00:00:56,360 --> 00:01:02,840
And the more you start to realize that it's actually part of the journey it is necessary to succeed.
你也会越来越意识到，失败是过程的一部分；她认为这是成功所需的经历。

12
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:08,321
If you're someone who wants to succeed at anything you don't have to be want to be a millionaire.
如果你想在某事上成功，不一定非得想成为百万富翁。

13
00:01:08,321 --> 00:01:13,120
But if you want to succeed at something at a career if you want to succeed on a path.
也许你希望事业成功，或在某条道路上取得进展。

14
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:18,721
You want to succeed at helping someone you want to succeed in any way shape or form you will fail.
也许你想帮助别人；在她看来，不论以什么形式追求成功，都难免失败。

15
00:01:18,721 --> 00:01:25,190
I need you to just be comfortable with the thought that failure is it's necessary.
她希望你能够接受失败是必要经历这一想法。

16
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:32,480
Every single person that you meet who you may find as successful has failed more times than you know.
你遇到的每个看似成功的人，可能都经历过比你知道的更多的失败。

17
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:37,361
Think about something you failed at did you learn something from it most likely yes.
想想你失败过的事情，你有没有从中学到什么？很可能有。

18
00:01:37,361 --> 00:01:41,551
If you failed in a relationship you learned how to look for a better one the next time.
如果一段关系失败，你可能学会下次寻找更适合的关系。

19
00:01:41,561 --> 00:01:44,241
Or how to show up as a better person the next time.
或者学会下次以更好的状态与人相处。

20
00:01:44,241 --> 00:01:48,561
If you failed at a job you probably learned to not make that mistake again.
如果工作上失败过，你可能学会不再犯同一个错误。

21
00:01:48,561 --> 00:01:52,961
Or you probably learned how to find a better job so on and so forth.
或者你学会了怎样找更好的工作，诸如此类。

22
00:01:52,961 --> 00:01:59,881
The faster you fail the faster you get to learn you need to know what works and what doesn't.
越快遇到失败，就越快学习；你要知道什么有效、什么无效。

23
00:01:59,881 --> 00:02:07,400
And it's honestly so freeing like the first few times that you fail because you're like okay that wasn't as bad I didn't die.
最初几次失败甚至可能让人释然：原来也没那么糟，我还好好的。

24
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:12,670
Each failure teaches you a valuable lesson that nothing else I promise you can teach you.
她说，每次失败都会教会你独特而宝贵的一课。

25
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:21,641
No amount of textbooks no amount of youtube videos that you watch could ever teach you any better than when you actually make mistakes yourself.
她认为，再多课本和视频也不如亲自犯错来得深刻。

26
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:26,760
Time is the most valuable thing and the the less time you waste.
时间最宝贵，你越少浪费时间……

27
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:30,840
On thinking of what could be or thinking about what you should start.
少纠结可能会怎样、自己究竟应该开始什么。

28
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:36,680
The sooner you can get to actually building experience building that knowledge building your skills.
就能越早积累经验、知识和技能。

29
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:43,241
You're speeding up the process to get to your dream life failure is not your enemy it is actually your friend.
你在加快接近理想生活的过程；她把失败比作朋友，而非敌人。

30
00:02:43,241 --> 00:02:52,040
Second on the list that I really really wish I knew as early as possible was that it's okay to be multifaceted.
她希望自己早点知道的第二点，是有多个面向也没关系。

31
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:58,641
It's okay to have multiple passions and multiple things that you're interested in it's actually an advantage.
有多种热爱、对不同事情感兴趣，她觉得这其实是优势。

32
00:02:58,641 --> 00:03:06,361
I really wish that somebody had given me the permission to be a multifaceted human being.
我真希望有人早些告诉我，可以允许自己成为多面的人。

33
00:03:06,361 --> 00:03:14,041
As someone who felt like I was there was something wrong with me because I couldn't pick a one career like a lot of my friends in high school did.
过去我觉得自己有问题，因为不能像很多高中朋友那样选定一个职业。

34
00:03:14,041 --> 00:03:18,640
You are going to be more likely to learn new skills multiple skills at the same time.
她认为多面向的人更可能同时学习多种技能。

35
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:26,081
You're going to broaden your network because you're going to meet so many different types of people people across different industries because you are multifaceted.
你还会接触来自不同行业的各种人，从而拓展人脉。
